# Industrial / Brutalist Frontend Craftsmanship

Brutalism is honesty executed with force. This pack speaks in ONE voice:
raw grids, abrupt energy, exposed structure, mechanical confidence.
(For cinematic restraint and slow editorial pacing, use the premium-luxury
pack instead — never blend the two.)

## Identity

- Feeling in five seconds: loud, deliberate, built. The site shows its bones.
- Structure IS the decoration. No ornament layered on top of it.
- One loud device per page — a marquee, a sticker collage, an oversized
  index — not five. Everything else is grid.

## Structural language

**Grid, visible.** The layout admits it is a grid: hard column rules,
elements butted flush against edges and each other, no polite gutters
hiding the seams. Masonry or strict columns — never cards floating in
soft space.

**Borders and shadows.** Thick 4px solid borders (black or ink) on all
major elements. Hard offset shadows, 4–8px, zero blur — the shadow is a
printed block, not a light source. Cards and badges may rotate -2deg/2deg
for sticker energy; nothing else tilts.

**Navigation.** Blunt: a bordered bar or an oversized index. Links are
uppercase text or bordered blocks that press when hit. No hiding-on-
scroll tricks — the nav is furniture, bolted down.

## Motion language — GSAP + Lenis only

GSAP (with ScrollTrigger — all plugins free) is the sole motion library
across every framework. Do not introduce Framer Motion, CSS keyframe
systems, or other animation libraries into a brutalist build.

Named values (tune in sketchbook reps — they are the signature):

- `press`: translateX/Y equal to the shadow offset, snapping flat on
  release — the mechanical press. Every clickable does it.
- `slam-in`: back.out(3) or steps-style snap, 0.25–0.4s — entrances land,
  they do not drift in.
- `ticker`: linear, looping — marquees only, pausable on hover/focus.
- Stagger: 0.05s, strict order — a machine feeding parts, not a cascade.

Rules:
- Abrupt by design: spring or linear timing, short durations, hard cuts.
  No slow fades, no eased drift, no parallax haze.
- State changes still transition (150–300ms) — mechanical, never
  instant-teleport, never mushy.
- Borders and offset shadows may move; blur and glow never appear.
- Reduced motion: `gsap.matchMedia()` with a calm variant — instant
  states, no transforms, marquees stopped.

## Typography & color

- Oversized grotesk or mono display set tight — `clamp()` up to ~10vw,
  uppercase welcome; body 16px+ and unapologetically plain, 60–75ch.
  Maximum 2 families.
- High-saturation color blocking on a flat ground (cream/paper works):
  2–3 loud hues + ink, all flat fills. Color shouts once per block; it
  never murmurs everywhere.
- No gradients, no texture overlays, no frosted glass. Surfaces are
  paint, not atmosphere.

## Performance imperative

A loud site that stutters is just noise.
- Composite only: animate `transform` and `opacity`. Never width, height,
  top, or margin. The press effect is pure translate.
- Zero layout shift from animation or hover — rotated elements reserve
  their rotated bounding box.
- Images flat and honest: AVIF/WebP, sized, lazy below fold.

## Accessibility floor

Loud is not an excuse.
- 4.5:1 contrast minimum, verified inside every color block — vivid
  yellow with white text fails; test the actual pairs.
- Visible focus states: a thick offset outline fits the voice — make
  focus the loudest state, not the missing one.
- Full keyboard paths — every press and marquee operable without a
  pointer. `cursor: pointer` on all clickables.

## Implementation ecosystem

- **React / Next.js:** `@gsap/react` (`useGSAP` for scoping/cleanup) +
  `lenis` where smooth scroll serves the grid; native scroll is also
  legitimate here — decide per project MASTER.md.
- **Astro / vanilla:** GSAP timelines + `lenis` (npm package `lenis` —
  the `@studio-freight/lenis` name is deprecated).

## Do not

- Corporate minimalism: quiet grays, hairline borders, whitespace-as-
  statement.
- Soft shadows, gradients, decorative blur, glassmorphism, glow.
- Rounded-pill CTAs — corners are square or barely eased.
- Emoji as icons; use SVG (Heroicons, Lucide) at consistent weight.
- Layout shift from animation. Ever.
